    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22085" root="شرخ" body-key="$">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَرَخَ</span></b> , (S, A, L, K,) aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَرَخَ</span></b> , (L,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَرْخٌ</span>
(S, K) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شُرُوخٌ</span>, (L, K,) said of the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَاب</span> [or
tush] of a camel, <i>It clave the flesh,</i> (S, A, * L, K,)
<i>and came forth.</i> (L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَرَخَ</span>, inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شُرُوخٌ</span>
(S, L) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَرْخٌ</span>, (L,) said of a boy, <i>He became a
youth,</i> or <i>young man, such as is termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَارِخٌ</span>.
(S, L.)

